  "worked_solution": "The powers of $2$ that are greater or equal to $1$ are\n\n$$\nE={1,2,4,8,16,32,64,\u2026}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, the powers of $4$ that are greater or equal to $1$ are\n\n$$\nF={1,4,16,64,256,\u2026}.\n$$\n\nNow, $F-E$ is the *difference* of $F$ and $E,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $F$ but *not* in $E.$\n\nAll elements of $F$ are also in $E.$  So, we must remove these elements from $F.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F-E & ={1,4,16,64,256,\u2026}-{1,2,4,8,16,32,64,\u2026} \\\\  & =\u2205.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
